config FLD_GPU
	bool "FLD frame-load GPU scheduler for Adreno (KGSL)"
	depends on QCOM_KGSL=y
	help
	  Frame Load Decision (FLD) is a GPU scheduler for Qualcomm Adreno
	  (KGSL) that picks GPU power levels from per-frame demand instead
	  of only reacting to averaged GPU busy time.  It combines GPU
	  feedback (hardware busy counters) with CPU feed-forward (PELT
	  utilization of the threads submitting GPU work), then tunes the
	  latency-adding parts of the KGSL power path (idle timer, power
	  level shaping) on top.

	  FLD is NOT a devfreq governor: there is nothing to select.  While
	  FLD is enabled it owns the GPU frequency decision and the stock
	  devfreq governor's requests are ignored; all thermal and user
	  constraints keep working.  /sys/kernel/fld/ exposes tunables and
	  runtime status.

	  Requires CONFIG_QCOM_KGSL=y (built-in).  Verified on Linux 4.19
	  (Adreno 610 / Snapdragon 680).  See docs/fld-kgsl-hooks.md for the
	  KGSL integration points this depends on.

config FLD_GPU_DEBUG
	bool "FLD verbose decision logging"
	depends on FLD_GPU
	help
	  Log every FLD frequency decision and idle-timer change with
	  pr_info_ratelimited().  Off by default; enable only while tuning,
	  this can be noisy under sustained GPU load.
